  "_about": "Every number in the explainer comes from here. Keys without a provenance of their own were measured on one Apple M4 Pro (10 P + 4 E cores, 128-byte cache lines, 128 KB L1D per P-core, 16 MB L2 per cluster), macOS, rustc 1.98.0, bench profile (fat LTO), threads not pinned, 2026-10-09/10. Units: M records/s unless a key says ns or us. Pairs are two rounds in separate processes. 'one_line' = both cursors in one 128-byte line (ring at 0 mod 128); 'two_lines' = cursors on separate lines (ring at 64 mod 128). Rings heap-placed at a fixed offset for the two-thread cells unless 'stock_harness' is noted. Keys measured later carry their own provenance (date, machine, build, commit or run): padding_128_m4, rtrb_against_ring_m4, issue_55_consumer_work_ci and ci_rebased_heads. Their M4 runs (2026-10-11/12) used rustc 1.97/1.98, the fat-LTO bench profile and loop heads pinned with -C llvm-args=-align-loops=16; their 'one_line' / 'two_lines' is the ring at byte 0 / 64 of a 256-byte block by the placement harness (#51). Ring = this repo's ring_spsc; rtrb = the rtrb 0.4 crate.",
